Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds app/modules/n8n/ (S3 of the n8n-workflows-page project): routers +
services + schemas mirroring the youtube module's shape (bare typed
responses, concrete response_model, Depends(get_current_user_org)).
Consumes the seed n8n adapter (feat/n8n-seed-adapter, this branch's
base) via a DI-seam client factory — never re-rolls HTTP, never lets
an incomplete credential silently degrade into FakeN8nClient data.

- workflows: list (client/unassigned scope) + assign/unassign
  (tag-preserving) + patch (rename/activate/folder-move) + delete +
  run (409 pre-check, zero side effects when blocked) + executions +
  tags.
- settings: GET derives status from the decrypted credential (never
  trusts the stored status column); PUT merges partial credential
  updates, resolves tag_id via a live lookup, and actively pings.
- folders: CRUD over the documented (not-yet-merged) n8n_folders /
  n8n_workflow_placement shape — cycle-guard (422), sibling-name
  conflict (409), delete-with-reassignment (absent reassign_to ⇒ root,
  per the FE's binding contract clarification).

app/main.py is untouched — a peer branch is live there; the tech-lead
wires MODULES at integration. 55 new tests, all green, run against the
worktree's own seed copy (verified via purge_shadowing_editable_finders
+ the running app's logged seed_version=runtime:fe52c096).

